From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play a tile's video over its picture's own place

A tile whose picture fits in it (maxSize: a collection's capture of
another shape than the card) played its video cut to the whole tile,
so the swap from the capture to the video jumped from the picture's
place to the tile's. The video now fills the picture's place, cut to
it, centred on the same point.
---
 es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp b/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
index a4a9b975..054056f1 100644
--- a/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/GridTileComponent.cpp
@@ -245,7 +245,13 @@ void GridTileComponent::resize()
 		{
 			mVideo->setOrigin(0.5, 0.5);			
 			mVideo->setPosition(imageOffset.x() + imageSize.x() / 2.0f, imageOffset.y() + imageSize.y() / 2.0f);
-			mVideo->setMinSize(imageSize.x(), imageSize.y());
+
+			// A picture fitted in the tile (maxSize) keeps its own place: the video fills that place, cut to it, so
+			// the swap from the picture to the video moves nothing
+			if (currentProperties.Image.sizeMode == "maxSize" && mImage != nullptr && mImage->getSize().x() > 0 && mImage->getSize().y() > 0)
+				mVideo->setMinSize(mImage->getSize().x(), mImage->getSize().y());
+			else
+				mVideo->setMinSize(imageSize.x(), imageSize.y());
 
 			if (mImage != nullptr)
 				mVideo->setRoundCorners(mImage->getRoundCorners());
